{"step_index":161,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T14:55:47Z","thinking":"Focus is shifting to redesigning the image inspection tab. The goal is to create an inspection gallery grid beneath the image upload area. This grid will offer filtering options for all, defective, passed, and uncertain images. Each image card will display the full image with a defect bounding box and a status badge within a styled 3-column layout.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Update Tab 1 to render an interactive multi-column card grid of all inspected units with defect bounding boxes and telemetry","EndLine":375,"Instruction":"Replace Tab 1 inspection results with a 3-column interactive gallery grid and analytics","ReplacementContent":"    # ── Upload & Batch Runner ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    uploaded_files = st.file_uploader(\n        \"Upload inspection image(s)\",\n        type=['jpg', 'jpeg', 'png', 'bmp', 'tiff'],\n        accept_multiple_files=True,\n        key=\"img_upload\",\n    )\n\n    if uploaded_files:\n        if not st.session_state.yolo_model:\n            st.error(\"❌ YOLOv8 model not loaded. Check sidebar.\")\n        else:\n            if st.button(\"▶ Run Visual Inspection on Batch\", type=\"primary\", use_container_width=True):\n                progress_bar = st.progress(0)\n                for i, f in enumerate(uploaded_files):\n                    img = Image.open(io.BytesIO(f.read())).convert('RGB')\n                    result = run_inference(img, st.session_state.yolo_model, conf_threshold)\n                    st.session_state.registry.add(f.name, result)\n                    st.session_state.annotated_images[f.name] = result\n                    progress_bar.progress((i + 1) / len(uploaded_files))\n\n                st.success(f\"✅ Successfully inspected {len(uploaded_files)} unit(s)!\")\n\n    # ── Results Section ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n    st.divider()\n    reg_df  = registry.to_dataframe()\n    summary = registry.summary()\n\n    if not reg_df.empty and st.session_state.annotated_images:\n        st.markdown(\"### 🖼️ Inspected Units Gallery & Defect Localization Grid\")\n        \n        # Filter buttons\n        filter_col1, filter_col2 = st.columns([1, 3])\n        with filter_col1:\n            gal_filter = st.selectbox(\n                \"Filter View\",\n                [\"All Units\", \"Defects Only (🔴)\", \"Passed Units (✅)\", \"Uncertain / Novel (🟡🟣)\"],\n                key=\"gal_filter_sel\",\n            )\n\n        # Filter items\n        items = list(st.session_state.annotated_images.items())\n        if gal_filter == \"Defects Only (🔴)\":\n            items = [it for it in items if it[1]['status'] == 'DEFECT']\n        elif gal_filter == \"Passed Units (✅)\":\n            items = [it for it in items if it[1]['status'] == 'PASS']\n        elif gal_filter == \"Uncertain / Novel (🟡🟣)\":\n            items = [it for it in items if it[1]['status'] in ('UNCERTAIN', 'NOVEL')]\n\n        if not items:\n            st.info(f\"No units match filter: '{gal_filter}'\")\n        else:\n            # Render in 3-column Grid\n            num_cols = 3\n            for row_idx in range(0, len(items), num_cols):\n                row_items = items[row_idx:row_idx + num_cols]\n                cols = st.columns(num_cols)\n                for col_idx, (fname, res) in enumerate(row_items):\n                    with cols[col_idx]:\n                        stat = res['status']\n                        dtype = res['defect_type'].upper()\n                        conf = res['confidence'] * 100\n                        bbox = res.get('bbox')\n                        \n                        # Card Container\n                        st.markdown(f\"\"\"\n<div style=\"background:#1a1f2e; border-radius:10px; padding:10px; border-top: 4px solid {'#e74c3c' if stat=='DEFECT' else '#2ecc71' if stat=='PASS' else '#f39c12'}; margin-bottom:12px;\">\n    <div style=\"display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; margin-bottom:6px;\">\n        <span style=\"font-weight:600; font-size:13px; color:#ecf0f1; overflow:hidden; text-overflow:ellipsis; white-space:nowrap; max-width:180px;\">{fname}</span>\n        <span class=\"badge badge-{stat}\">{stat}</span>\n    </div>\n</div>\n\"\"\", unsafe_allow_html=True)\n                        if res.get('annotated_image'):\n                            st.image(res['annotated_image'], use_container_width=True)\n\n                        st.markdown(f\"**Defect:** `{dtype}` &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Conf:** `{conf:.1f}%`\")\n                        if bbox:\n                            x1, y1, x2, y2 = [int(v) for v in bbox]\n                            st.caption(f\"📍 Box: `[{x1}, {y1}, {x2}, {y2}]` ({x2-x1}×{y2-y1}px)\")\n                        else:\n                            st.caption(\"✅ Surface clean / within tolerance\")\n\n        st.divider()\n\n        # ── Summary Charts & Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────\n        st.markdown(\"### 📊 Batch Quality Analytics & Inspection Log\")\n        r1, r2 = st.columns([1, 2])\n\n        with r1:\n            st.plotly_chart(defect_donut(summary), use_container_width=True, key=\"quality_donut_chart\")\n            if summary.get('by_type'):\n                st.plotly_chart(defect_type_bar(summary['by_type']), use_container_width=True, key=\"quality_type_bar_chart\")\n\n        with r2:\n            st.markdown(\"#### Detailed Inspection Table\")\n            styled = reg_df.copy()\n            styled['Status'] = styled['status'].apply(\n                lambda s: f\"🔴 {s}\" if s == 'DEFECT'\n                else (f\"✅ {s}\" if s == 'PASS'\n                else (f\"🟡 {s}\" if s == 'UNCERTAIN' else f\"🟣 {s}\"))\n            )\n            st.dataframe(\n                styled[['unit_id', 'image_name', 'defect_type', 'co