{"step_index":165,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T14:56:06Z","content":"### 🚀 Updates & Fixes Applied\n\n---\n\n### 1. 🔍 Fixed Defect Bounding Boxes for `rust` & `scratch`\n- **Removed the Oversized Fallback Frame**: Previously, when scratch lines (which are thin) or rust spots were filtered out by generic blob-area thresholds, an artificial fallback box was drawn spanning 60% of the image frame (making it look cropped/zoomed in).\n- **Specialized Scratch Filter**: Added a **BlackHat + TopHat morphological ridge filter** that isolates thin surface scratch lines directly, drawing a tight, localized bounding box directly over the scratch groove.\n- **Specialized Rust Filter**: Implemented adaptive **HSV & LAB color deviation clustering** to identify the concentrated rust patch, strictly capped to prevent stretching across the entire frame.\n- **Peak Anomaly Anchoring**: If a defect is subtle, the bounding box anchors tightly around the **exact peak anomaly $(cx, cy)$ coordinate** with compact dimensions ($20\\%$ radius), so it never covers the whole image.\n\n---\n\n### 2. 🖼️ Multi-Column Interactive Card Grid\n- All inspected images are now displayed in a **clean, 3-column responsive inspection grid** rather than a single vertical list.\n- Each unit card displays:\n  - The annotated image with its targeted bounding box and HUD corner target brackets.\n  - **Filename & Color-Coded Status Badge** (`🔴 DEFECT`, `✅ PASS`, `🟡 UNCERTAIN`, `🟣 NOVEL`).\n  - **Defect Class Tag & Model Confidence %** (e.g. `SCRATCH · 98.4%`).\n  - **Pixel Bounding Box Coordinates & Area** (e.g. `[124, 88, 210, 160] (86×72px)`).\n- **Interactive View Filter**: Switch between `All Units`, `Defects Only`, `Passed Units`, and `Uncertain / Novel`.\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ To Run the Updated System:\nSimply refresh your browser tab, or run:\n```powershell\ncd C:\\Users\\win-10\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\neurax_app\npython -m streamlit run app.py\n```"}
