{"step_index":167,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T15:14:40Z","thinking":"The user reports a problem with incorrect highlighting in a rust and scratch scenario using a YOLOv8 model. The core hypothesis is that the model type might be incorrect: specifically, perhaps a classification model was used instead of an object detection model. It is essential to determine which YOLOv8 variant was trained and deployed.\n\n\nThe model's behavior hinges on whether it's a classifier or a detector. A classification model, indicated by the presence of `result.probs`, won't generate bounding boxes directly; instead, classical computer vision techniques are used to localize defects, which can be prone to errors with complex textures. Conversely, a detection model, identified by `result.boxes`, should output accurate bounding boxes natively. Therefore, the discrepancy likely stems from using the wrong model type or from using the custom localization method when a YOLO-generated box is available. The direct use of the YOLO's plotting function `result.plot()` would render the YOLO-generated boxes if `result.boxes` is populated.\n\n\nA key check is whether `result.boxes` exists, indicating an object detection model; if present, YOLO's native boxes are used. If `result.probs` exists instead, this indicates a classification model, which lacks bounding boxes. In the classification case, a misleading synthetic box should not be drawn; instead, a classification card with probability breakdowns or a heatmap visualization should be presented.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python -c \"\nimport os\nfrom utils.constants import MODEL_PATHS\nfor p in MODEL_PATHS:\n    print(f'Checking {p}: exists = {os.path.exists(p)}')\n\"","Cwd":"C:\\Users\\win-10\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\neurax_app","WaitMsBeforeAsync":3000,"toolAction":"Checking model files","toolSummary":"Check best.pt paths"}}]}
